C LB-relaxed
"Plain relaxed load buffering (no dependencies, no thin-air value invention). RC11
 enforces the no-thin-air axiom acyclic(po | rf), which forbids ALL load-buffering
 shapes, so RC11 reports Never. C++20 did NOT adopt that axiom (P0668 fixed seq_cst
 but deliberately left thin-air unresolved), so C++20 -- exactly like C11/C++17 --
 permits this LB. The C++20 side is modelled with herd7's original C11 model
 (c11_orig.cat), whose relaxed/thin-air fragment C++20 leaves unchanged => Sometimes.
   herd7 -model rc11.cat     => Never      (RC11 forbids)
   herd7 -model c11_orig.cat => Sometimes  (C++20, via the unchanged C11 fragment)"
{ int x=0; int y=0; }
P0 (atomic_int* x, atomic_int* y) {
  int r1 = atomic_load_explicit(x,memory_order_relaxed);
  atomic_store_explicit(y,1,memory_order_relaxed);
}
P1 (atomic_int* x, atomic_int* y) {
  int r2 = atomic_load_explicit(y,memory_order_relaxed);
  atomic_store_explicit(x,1,memory_order_relaxed);
}
exists (0:r1=1 /\ 1:r2=1)
